+
+<section xml:id=3D"cll_chapter17-section20">
+  <title>20. Proposed lerfu words for radio communication</title>
+  <para>There is a set of English words which are used, by international a=
greement, as lerfu words (for the English alphabet) over the radio, or in n=
oisy situations where the utmost clarity is required. Formally they are kno=
wn as the =E2=80=9CICAO Phonetic Alphabet=E2=80=9D, and are used even in no=
n-English-speaking countries.</para>
