re not Lojban consonants: the =E2=80=9Cch=E2=80=9D of =E2=80=9Cchurch=E2=80=
=9D and the =E2=80=9Cj=E2=80=9D of =E2=80=9Cjudge=E2=80=9D. In Lojban, thes=
e are considered two consonant sounds spoken together without an intervenin=
g vowel sound, and so are represented in Lojban by the two separate consona=
